er for White to defend.\n\nTherefore, **I11** is the most aggressive and structurally sound move, creating an immediate threat while maximizing future winning chances along the I-column and diagonals.\n\nReason: Black plays I11 to form a diagonal Open 3 (Live 3) with stones G9 and H10. This forces White to defend. Unlike playing the forced 4s at F9 or H11 immediately, this move preserves those threats for a later combination attack and opens up the unblocked I-column for vertical expansion.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "I", "row": 11}'}
